#!/bin/bash
# A stand-in claude for the demo: it draws the screen a real one would show,
# close enough that agent-scan reads its state the same way, and never talks
# to anything. Its name is what makes agent-scan take it for claude.
#
# AGENT_DEMO_SCENE picks the screen:
#
#   running   works on AGENT_DEMO_TASK, at AGENT_DEMO_STEP, for
#             AGENT_DEMO_SECONDS (default 12), then finishes with
#             AGENT_DEMO_REPLY
#   blocked   asks to make an edit, and waits; 1 or 2 says yes, and it
#             goes on at AGENT_DEMO_NEXT_STEP and finishes with
#             AGENT_DEMO_NEXT_REPLY
#   done      has finished with AGENT_DEMO_REPLY
#
# Started with no scene - as the sidebar's new worktree starts it - it runs
# a short task of its own and finishes.

scene="${AGENT_DEMO_SCENE:-running}"
task="${AGENT_DEMO_TASK:-look around the new worktree}"
reply="${AGENT_DEMO_REPLY:-Ready. The worktree builds and its tests pass.}"
step="${AGENT_DEMO_STEP:-Reading the code this touches}"
seconds="${AGENT_DEMO_SECONDS:-12}"
branch="$(git branch --show-current 2>/dev/null)"
started="${SECONDS}"
frames=('·' '✢' '✳' '✶' '✻' '✽')

# Not tr: it swaps bytes, and ─ is three of them.
rule() {
    local line
    printf -v line '%*s' "$(tput cols)" ''
    printf '\e[2m%s\e[0m\n' "${line// /─}"
}

footer() {
    rule
    printf '\e[1m❯\e[0m\n'
    rule
    printf '  \e[2m⎇ %s | (+%s,-%s)   Model: Opus 5 | Ctx: %s\e[0m\n' \
        "${branch:-main}" "$1" "$2" "$3"
    printf '  \e[2m⏵⏵ bypass permissions on (shift+tab to cycle)\e[0m\n'
}

prompt() {
    printf '\e[2J\e[H'
    printf '\e[1m❯\e[0m %s\n\n' "${task}"
}

draw_running() {
    local elapsed=$((SECONDS - started)) frame
    frame="${frames[elapsed % ${#frames[@]}]}"
    prompt
    printf '\e[1m●\e[0m %s\n' "${step}"
    printf '  \e[2m⎿  Read 4 files\e[0m\n\n'
    printf '\e[38;5;209m%s Working… (%ss · ↓ %s.%sk tokens)\e[0m\n' \
        "${frame}" "${elapsed}" "$((elapsed / 3 + 1))" "$((elapsed % 10))"
    footer "$((elapsed * ${#task} / 5))" "$((elapsed * ${#step} / 9))" "$((40 + elapsed)).2k"
}

draw_done() {
    prompt
    printf '\e[1m●\e[0m %s\n\n' "${reply}"
    printf '\e[2m✻ Worked for 3m 12s · done %s\e[0m\n' "$(date '+%-I:%M %p')"
    # Changes and context that differ from one agent to the next.
    footer "$((${#reply} * 3))" "$((${#task} / 2))" "$((${#reply} + 20)).4k"
}

draw_blocked() {
    prompt
    printf '\e[1m●\e[0m The limiter goes in front of every public route.\n\n'
    rule
    printf ' \e[1mEdit file\e[0m\n'
    printf ' src/middleware/limits.ts\n'
    printf ' \e[31m 12 -  return next();\e[0m\n'
    printf ' \e[32m 12 +  return limiter.check(req) ? next() : tooMany(res);\e[0m\n'
    printf ' Do you want to make this edit to limits.ts?\n'
    printf ' \e[38;5;117m❯ 1. Yes\e[0m\n'
    printf '   2. Yes, and switch to accept edits for this session (shift+tab)\n'
    printf '   3. No\n'
    printf ' \e[2mEsc to cancel · Tab to amend\e[0m\n'
}

draw() {
    case "${scene}" in
    running) draw_running ;;
    blocked) draw_blocked ;;
    *) draw_done ;;
    esac
}

printf '\e[?25l'
trap draw WINCH
while :; do
    if [[ "${scene}" == running ]] && ((SECONDS - started >= seconds)); then
        scene="done"
    fi
    draw
    # A running screen ticks; the rest wait for a key, and redraw on resize.
    key=""
    if [[ "${scene}" == running ]]; then
        read -rsn1 -t 1 key || true
    else
        read -rsn1 key || true
    fi
    if [[ "${scene}" == blocked && "${key}" == [12] ]]; then
        scene=running started="${SECONDS}" seconds=6
        step="${AGENT_DEMO_NEXT_STEP:-Applying the edit}"
        reply="${AGENT_DEMO_NEXT_REPLY:-Done.}"
    fi
done
